# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Attestrum working directory (created by `attestrum build` / `attestrum init`)
.attestrum/

# Editor + tooling caches
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Local-only env files (never check in secrets)
.env
.env.local

# Python venvs (in case cross-check tooling lands locally)
/venv/
/.venv/

# Claude Code per-project local state (scheduled-task lockfiles, etc.)
.claude/

# Locally-rendered PNG diagrams (see CLAUDE.md §2 + tools/render-diagrams.sh).
# Mermaid sources under docs/diagrams/ are authoritative; PNGs are derived
# convenience artifacts (slides, partner emails, print) and never committed.
/diagrams-png/

# Local-only brand assets (video/audio/logo source files for marketing).
# Kept on the local filesystem only; never versioned. Safety-net entry so a
# future `git add -A` can't accidentally sweep them in.
/Branding Material/

# Playwright MCP browser-session cache (console logs, page snapshots).
# Local-only; never versioned.
/.playwright-mcp/

# Credential / private-key filename patterns. Hard denylist enforced by
# git (independent of any agent reading CLAUDE.md). See CLAUDE.md §0.5
# Publication Boundary + tools/secret-scanner/ for content-level scanning.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt.key
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
id_dsa
id_dsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
credentials
credentials.*
secrets
secrets.*
*.token
*.session
*.cookie
*-private.md
*.private

# Safety net: any path containing "internal-notes" stays out. The canonical
# internal-only location is ~/Documents/Claude/Attestrum-internal-notes/
# (outside this repo), but this catches a stray symlink or copy-by-mistake.
**/internal-notes/
**/internal-notes-*/
*internal-notes*

# Test / claude-code session artifacts that aren't already excluded
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/

# Removed canonical files (CLAUDE.md §0.5.2). These three were removed
# from the tree during the 2026-05-25 public-release cleanup; they are
# retained as local-only notes at ~/Documents/Claude/Attestrum-internal-notes/.
# Listing them by exact root-name prevents a stale-instruction agent
# (e.g., a session pointed at a pre-cleanup plan file) from re-creating
# them via `git add SESSION-LOG.md`. The leading `/` anchors to the
# repo root only — legitimate references to these names inside other
# files (migration notes, diagram prose) are unaffected.
/SESSION-LOG.md
/BUILD-PLAN.md
/PATH-A-BRIEF.md
